On Saturday evening, the doorbell rings.
I open the door and Sabine is standing there with Bruno.
The small dog immediately wags his tail.
"Come in, the food is ready!" I say.
We sit down at the table in my flat.
I serve the Mexican food.
Sabine tastes it and smiles.
"This tastes fantastic, Maya!" she says.
"Thank you very much for the invitation."
While we eat, Bruno lies quietly under the table.
Later I fetch the dessert.
We drink tea and talk about January.
The weather was so cold and grey back then.
We remember our first meeting in the stairwell.
"You didn't even have a winter coat!" laughs Sabine.
"Yes, only a light jacket," I answer.
Back then we didn't know each other at all and addressed each other formally.
Today in the summer we sit together as good friends.
The cold January is really far away now.
